<title>JAPAN: Japan Feb aluminium imports up 8.7 pct yr/yr--MOF.</title>
<headline>Japan Feb aluminium imports up 8.7 pct yr/yr--MOF.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's refined aluminium imports totalled 234,648 tonnes in February, up 8.7 percent from 215,802 tonnes in the same month last year, Finance Ministry statistics released on Friday showed.</p>
<p>The following is a breakdown (on a customs-cleared basis, in tonnes):</p>
<p>		    Feb 97    Jan 97	Feb 96</p>
<p> Total	   234,648   230,552     215,802</p>
<p>Major suppliers:</p>
<p> Brazil	   18,038    24,657	42,810</p>
<p> Russia	   54,816    38,589	36,984</p>
<p> Australia	41,594    39,896	36,955</p>
<p> U.S.	     11,593    10,232	15,909</p>
<p>Cumulative imports of refined aluminium in the first two months of 1997 were 465,200 tonnes, up from 413,882 tonnes in the same period a year earlier.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk +81-3-3432-6179</p>
</text>
